# @bunki/ai — environment template (WP-07; controller §9, §15, REQ-AI-03).
#
# THIS FILE IS COMMITTED AND MUST NEVER CONTAIN A VALUE.
# Copy it to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill that in, or export the variables in
# the shell that runs the process. `.env` is ignored by the repository root
# .gitignore; `.env.example` is the one file explicitly un-ignored.
#
# A key must never reach a client bundle. On the Phase-0 Expo Web target there
# is no `process`, so the app cannot read one and every request takes the
# labelled `offline-fallback` route — which is the correct behaviour, not a
# degraded one. The live path is for a host that has an environment: a test
# runner, a script, or a future server-side gateway.
#
# Operator gate: controller §22.3 (OD-08). Until the operator provides a key and
# a budget cap, live-call evidence stays OPEN in the build capsule and no test
# in this repository makes a network call.

# Anthropic Messages API key. Required for the live route; absent = fallback.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to the model pinned in src/provider/anthropic.ts.
BUNKI_AI_MODEL=
